A||||46||GT Bastard||So who's got their own philosophy on life?||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-29-2001||11:45 PM||||I always think it's interesting to hear how other people view life, and what their basic philosophy is.  Generally people seem to think I'm easy going(although forum members probably think I'm a hot-headed psycho because I find flames amusing.)  I wish I could say that I've come to some sort of conclusion about how life should be lived, but I'm only 20... Maybe I'll have it all figured out when I'm 21?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It always pains me the think of all the time I spent in school, and then thinking of the fact that nothing I ever learned can tell me how to be happy.<P>later kiddies...<P>ps-rum and mt. dew tastes like crap.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||03-30-2001||12:05 AM||||Vodka and Mountain Dew tastes even worse...<P>My philosophy?  Be happy.  Find what you love to do and do it.  Life isn't worth living otherwise.  And live for the now.  Don't waste your time planning for the future, or dwelling on the past.  It's not worth it, it leads to unhappiness.  I know I'll never be rich, but so what?  Too many people spend their time in the rat race scrambling for that extra buck that they forget how to live..  nothing can tell <B>you</B> how to be happy, you have to find out for yourself.<P>Oh yeah, I'm only 20 too.  Well, I'll be 20 in about 5 days...<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||03-30-2001||01:13 AM||||some of my philosophies:<P>For School:<BR>Beat the average<P>For life:<BR>Don't ask,don't get<P>what the he!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||03-30-2001||01:13 AM||||Ooooh, I like this topic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>First off, I'm only 20 years old as well, so I know I still got alot to learn.  But my basic Philosophy on life is to learn as much as I can.  I strive to be open-minded about everything and I never turn down a chance to do or meet anything or anyone new.  Along with this, I have no opinion on most things.  I like to be able to argue both sides of any situation.  But I also respect and listen to other peoples' opinions.  I respect everything, my friends, my enemies, my parents, my pets, and all people and animals, or at least I try to, no one is perfect.  <BR>But am i happy?  No, nor do I strive to be.  But I am not sad either.  I try to be in a comfortable medium.  I am also for the most part a "loner"  I have few friends, and I really don't like having alot of friends.  Most importantly though, I am content in my life.  I feel that I am living a good life and I am learning as much as I can about life so I can help other people with theirs.  <BR>Actually, my philosophy on life can be summed up in 3 words.<P>"Live and Learn"||||reg||7
Z||000004||terryk||03-30-2001||01:53 AM||||Frizbitarian....<P>I believe that when you die, your soul goes up on the roof and you can't get it down.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||03-30-2001||01:55 AM||||Whattaya know, I'm 20 also.. hehe..<P>my life's philosophies are a bit complicated to type put here, especially since I should be working on my research project that's due next thursday..<P>ask me again sometime.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||03-30-2001||02:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B>I strive to be open-minded about everything and I never turn down a chance to do or meet anything or anyone new.  Along with this, I have no opinion on most things.  I like to be able to argue both sides of any situation.  But I also respect and listen to other peoples' opinions.  I respect everything, my friends, my enemies, my parents, my pets, and all people and animals, or at least I try to, no one is perfect.  <BR>But am i happy?  No, nor do I strive to be.  But I am not sad either.  I try to be in a comfortable medium.  I am also for the most part a "loner"  I have few friends, and I really don't like having alot of friends.  Most importantly though, I am content in my life.  I feel that I am living a good life and I am learning as much as I can about life so I can help other people with theirs.  <BR>Actually, my philosophy on life can be summed up in 3 words.<P>"Live and Learn"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly man.   Whenever I try to put something down on paper (or screen) I know I lose at least half of what I'm trying to say...And I always lose something in the translation.. but this is exactly how I live too.  I guess I shouldn't say be happy, but happiness is a byproduct of living this way, at least for me it is.  And not the generic giddy laughing happy, but an overall good, content feeling about your life.  I think that alot of problems, if not all of them, are caused by a lack of respect, and being closed-minded.  <P>K, I think I fried a few brain cells trying to think too hard about this... that's another thing you can't do too much of, thinking.  You'll just end up hurting yourself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
