Z||000009||JohnnyK||03-30-2001||03:21 AM||||Life is a big, long road of hurt and suffering..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> No one knows why, and even though it shouldn't be (all your circumstances are great), it is anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Kelvin Vivian||03-30-2001||05:02 AM||||Well there's both a conservative philosophy and a liberal philosophy.<P>Conservatives believe that there exist moral absolutes, that individual actions are either right or wrong, and wish to apply their moral standard onto others. Which is fine.<P>Liberals believe, that there are moral rights and wrongs too, however they only apply their moral standard to themselves. Which is fine.<P>I say if you are liberal, be conservative when among conservatives (i.e. when in Rome, do as the Romans), and if you are conservative, judge not.<P>Conservatives like things the way they are, liberals are more open to change.<P>My goal is to be like Homer Simpson, marry a good woman and have three kids.  I like Fieros and playing soccer...<P>Watch "The Lion King", and learn about the Circle of Life...<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||03-30-2001||10:58 AM||||Beer... the cause of, and solution to, all of life's problems.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||03-30-2001||11:40 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kelvin Vivian:<BR><B>Liberals believe, that there are moral rights and wrongs too, however they only apply their moral standard to themselves. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, this sounds more like a Libertarian philosophy, to me. <BR>I profess to be Libertarian.<P>I try to treat people the way I'd like to be treated. I believe that whatever comes around, goes around. In this life or the next.<BR>I try to stay out of other people's business.<BR>I expect -no, insist -that other people stay out of <I>my</I> business.<BR>If people disagree with me, that's cool.<BR>If people try to force an opinion on me, without considering <I>my</I> right to disagree, they will lose credibility in my eyes.<BR>Like some conservatives, I have strong opinions about what is right or wrong. However, I will not force those opinions on other people. I may <I>express</I> my opinion, however (occasionally, sarcastically). If someone continues to do something that offends my sensibilities, I will simply choose to not be around that person. We are given a choice and a free will, and as I mentioned earlier, I believe that we will ultimately be responsible for what we do. <BR>Am I happy? Pretty much. Most of the time.<BR>Very infrequently am I profoundly unhappy. <BR>If I ever start feeling sorry for myself, I try to remind myself that things could always be <I>much</I> worse.<BR>I'm 44, BTW.<P>[/speech]<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000013||Philphine||03-30-2001||02:06 PM||||the one i like best:<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.<P>couple others i like:<P>i have to blow my own horn 'cause no one else can play it as well.<P>start slow...taper off.<P>love is a condition in which another persons happiness is essential to your own.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||frontal lobe||03-30-2001||02:13 PM||||Here are a few practical ones that could apply to anyone:<P>Drive a manual transmission as long as you are physically able.<P>Avoid mirrors.<P>Wear natural fibers if at all possible.<P>This meal may be your last-eat like it.<P>If you want to make a major purchase, (especially on credit), make yourself wait 2 weeks and then if you still want it, buy it.<P>DON'T make permanent markings on yourself because you know you like variety.<P>Oh yeah.  Almost forgot.  Just because something is true doesn't mean you have to say it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by frontal lobe (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||03-30-2001||03:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>   Actually, this sounds more like a Libertarian philosophy, to me. <BR>I profess to be Libertarian.<P>I try to treat people the way I'd like to be treated. I believe that whatever comes around, goes around. In this life or the next.<BR>I try to stay out of other people's business.<BR>I expect -no, insist -that other people stay out of <I>my</I> business.<BR>If people disagree with me, that's cool.<BR>If people try to force an opinion on me, without considering <I>my</I> right to disagree, they will lose credibility in my eyes.<BR>Like some conservatives, I have strong opinions about what is right or wrong. However, I will not force those opinions on other people. I may <I>express</I> my opinion, however (occasionally, sarcastically). If someone continues to do something that offends my sensibilities, I will simply choose to not be around that person. We are given a choice and a free will, and as I mentioned earlier, I believe that we will ultimately be responsible for what we do. <BR>Am I happy? Pretty much. Most of the time.<BR>Very infrequently am I profoundly unhappy. <BR>If I ever start feeling sorry for myself, I try to remind myself that things could always be <I>much</I> worse.<BR>I'm 44, BTW.<P>[/speech]<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That pretty much sums up 90% of my philosophy..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
