Z||000030||Patrick's Dad||04-01-2001||11:30 PM||||I'm the old man around here, it seems. Nigh unto 36....<P>When I was 20, my philosophy was "(CENSORED) 'em if they can't take a joke."<P>Now that I'm older, so much older (There's that darned music again!), it's the age old, "Love your neighbor more than yourself." Or, to quote Kirk insead of Christ;<P>Edith: "Whatever the trouble you may be in, let me help."<BR>Kirk: "Let me help.... A hundred years from now a poet will recommend those three words even over I love you."<BR>Edith: "A hundred years from now. Who...? Where will he come from?"<BR>Kirk: "A silly question, want a silly answer? From a planet circling that far left star in Orion's belt."<P>Of course, Edith gets killed by a car in just a couple of minutes, because Kirk keeps McCoy from helping.... Then again, all you twenty year olds are too young to remember this stuff, aren't you?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The point is, if you (any you) are more important to me than I am, then I'll naturally attend to your needs first, especially if you're in trouble. If we all thought this way (And no, I don't do it perfectly. I'm a student of "Tough Love" when it comes to money....), then we'd have substantially fewer problems in the world today.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/StarHeroSig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
